--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.inhctor.init]/1: `D a(5)' with `using B::B;' initializes the
B subobject by B(int) and the rest of D as a defaulted default constructor
of D would: k from its default member initializer, mm by M(), and D's
virtual table pointer.  The front end called B's constructor on the D
object directly, so none of that happened.  It now declares, for each
inherited constructor, a constructor of D whose mem-initializer forwards
the arguments to B's ([namespace.udecl]/11: one with the parameter-type-
list of D's own constructor is hidden).  bin53 rejects the program
(`D h("x", 9L)' does not uniquely resolve).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
